  "_signedOutOnlyComment": [
    "Routes that only exist for a SIGNED-OUT visitor. Both call supabase.auth.getUser()",
    "on mount and router.replace() away when a session exists, so a signed-in sweep",
    "measures an empty document: /login rendered 0 text elements, /signup 0.",
    "",
    "They stay in `public` and are fully measured by the signed-out sweeps. This list",
    "exists so the --auth sweep can SUBTRACT them, rather than reporting 'fewer than",
    "5 visible text elements' forever on pages that are behaving correctly.",
    "",
    "Do NOT 'fix the login page'. There is nothing wrong with it — bouncing a",
    "signed-in user off the login page is the point."
  ],
  "signedOutOnly": [
    "/login",
    "/signup"
  ],
  "authGated": {
